tive failures and cap it at 3, showing a failure toast and halting playback if exceeded, resetting the counter on any successful URL fetch. I'm also noticing a potential race: when a song fails and playNext is triggered immediately, the original failing song's async pic-fetch and save calls might still resolve afterward and overwrite the newly playing song's saved state, since fetching the next song's URL takes longer than the immediate failure handling.\n\nI'll fix this minimally by returning right after playNext() in the no-url branch so stale pic/save calls don't fire for a song that never played. For exiting FM, I need to update the bottom bar's song/artist/cover info before fetching the play URL, so I'll set AppStorage values directly in the FM exit logic ahead of calling playQueue.\n\nOn infinite-loop risk: a failing FM next-song request could cascade through retries, but the 3-consecutive-failure cap should stop it before it spirals. For the completion handler, FM mode should just call fmNext(), though I'm now second-guessing whether prefetching the next song on playback start adds too much complexity given the \"only one request in flight\" constraint — a prefetch would need to count against that limit.\n\nPrefetching also raises concurrency edge cases: if the user hits next while a prefetch is still in flight, the system has to wait for that existing request instead of firing a duplicate one, which complicates the single-request-in-flight guarantee I wanted to keep simple.\n\nI'll keep prefetch simple: once an FM song starts playing and it's the last in que","startTime":1792299988559,"lastModifiedTime":1792300012052},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01SpT6tmkwsB8sfZRqBV95Zz","type":"TOOL","toolName":"read_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec34/entry/src/main/ets/common/functions/play/playListOp.ets"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"<file>\n     1→import { LogUtil } from \"@pura/harmony-utils\"\n     2→import { putPla