er_enter.jpeg","absolutePath":"/tmp/fmscratch/after_enter.jpeg","resolution":"absolute","content":{"$blob":"sha256:3617a155572881ec658f81f649105b3a73030332ecde8db1551d623cad23274b","version":1,"encoding":"json","byteLength":251631,"compression":"none"},"isImage":true}}}]},{"id":"6ad4594e3e412730c6999795","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":32720},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"d3eacbf4-b9ad-4dc9-90a9-53d67133d48c","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"The entry flow checks out: card shows first, then the badge appears in the bottom bar within a second while the song \"高雅且隐晦\" plays, with the song name taking the remaining row space via layoutWeight so the badge sits spaced to the right. Now I'll move on to writing the Hypium test.\n\nI'm planning out the test files: one covering entry behavior (card visibility without scrolling, click-to-badge transition, song changes, no slider, rapid clicks), one for the player (badge, dislike, loop button swap, mode menu with its three options, cancel behavior, switching to explore mode, disliking a song), one for the manual queue (built via searching and playing songs individually since daily recommendations need login, then verifying the FM queue tip, exit button, and that exiting restores the original queue), one for restart behavior (badge and queue tip persisting through restart, exit restoring normal mode), and one for autoplay-next behavior by dragging the progress slider near the end.\n\nFor the no-API edge case, I'm weighing options since I can't easily stop the backend server from the test sandbox — maybe I can simulate it by temporarily pointing the app's API URL to something invalid through the settings page and then restoring it afterward, though that adds complexity I'll tackle last. Before that, I want to inspect the UI dumps for the queue sheet and player screens to understand their structure, then build a shared helper module with functions for launching, ensuring normal mode, opening/closing the