6b0b527c55b3a7982c2873e9","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":54167,"compression":"none"},"askReview":false,"diff":{"add":1,"remove":1},"runMode":"auto"}},"accepted":true,"isRebuilt":false}]},{"id":"6ad47b733e412730c69a03d3","discard":false,"metrics":{"duration":18845},"hasUnpairedToolUse":false,"children":[{"id":"5eaabf80-4b29-4ec2-a574-5cb3d986b4ce","type":"REASON","end":true,"content":"Now I'm thinking through the test setup, specifically adding a helper to count hilog entries matching a pattern by running the hilog command through the device shell, while being mindful that the hilog buffer may only hold a limited number of lines.\n\nFor the actual test assertions, I'm planning expected log deltas for each scenario: entering FM plays a song should produce exactly one request-fm log line within a few seconds, rapid clicks should still only produce one, re-clicking while already in FM should produce zero, and navigation away shouldn't trigger anything. For the player controls, cancelling the menu or reselecting the current song should have zero delta, switching to explore mode should produce one line containing the explore marker, disliking a song should add one trash-log entry, rapid dislikes should still only log once, skipping to next should add at most one entry, and exiting the queue or restarting the app should show zero delta for both log patterns at startup.\n\nOne caveat I'm flagging is that if a song is near its end, a near-end prefetch could unexpectedly fire mid-test and pollute the counts, though this is low risk given the short test duration and song lengths — though I need to consider whether songs resume from where they left off after a restart, which could increase that risk.\n\nNow I'm thinking through adding a cycle-mode test: looping through several iterations where I exit FM, open the player, toggle the loop button, close the player, re-enter FM, open the player again, drag the progress bar near the end, wait for the song to change, and check the badge each time — though this would take a long time across four iterations, and I don't have a way to directly verify the cycle mode icon without deeper accessibility inspection, which I'll skip for now. Since single-cycle mode could cause the same song to replay instead of advancing, running all four iterations is worth it to catch that specific failure case.\n\nI'm also considering whether the UI test environment supports screen rotation — the app's config doesn't explicitly declare orientation support, and phone defaults are typically portrait-locked unless auto-rotation is set, so I want to do a quick probe using the display rotation API to confirm before relying on it, and I'll start by writing a small helper function for that check.\n\n","startTime":1792310136792,"lastModifiedTime":1792310149531},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_015MmmZCFWjQAKkpR9BkftZt","type":"TOOL","toolName":"edit_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec34/hypium_tests/fm_helpers.py","new_string":{"$blob":"sha256:8f9e8293948abe97480fc83d753fec55cf66096d1e005561c3a03640e04cc5a1","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":466,"compression":"none"},"old_string":{"$blob":"sha256:f5119a8df71bf5e0138d4028d0539f3cfcadf1aa8f973fb21eec53436d8d441d","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":73,"compression":"none"}},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"relativePath":"hypium_tests/fm_helpers.py","absolutePath":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec34/hypium_tests/fm_helpers.py","resolution":"absolute","content":{"$blob":"sha256:ecf56aa71bce3e36ecb289e16b408e59464b5a98bb1901a6a1e5d6b241bac19c","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":7656,"compression":"none"},"originalContent":{"$blob":"sha256:a062ec4cd50941b3e65aa2f8b4d4fefe89aa0aca700eb9bbe197a93df2610fe5","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":7263,"compression":"none"},"askReview":false,"diff":{"add":11,"remove":0},"runMode":"auto"}},"accepte