amp after the index has already moved to the new song—could be what's causing a second premature prefetch call to fire.\n\nMy proposed fix is to track which index actually \"started\" playback via an onPlayStarted callback that fires only after setUrl completes for the current song, then gate onProgress to only act when the queue's current index matches that started index. This way, leftover timeUpdate events from the previous song get ignored instead of triggering an erroneous prefetch.\n\nBetter to track by song id instead of queue index — I'll have onPlayStarted take the song id and compare that against the currently started song id during progress checks, avoiding stale-index issues. Resetting on switch isn't needed since the id comparison naturally handles it.\n\n","startTime":1792312725886,"lastModifiedTime":1792312739290},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01U11eUyvxNfy39SQfoHXZPT","type":"TOOL","toolName":"edit_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec34/entry/src/main/ets/common/utils/play/FMUtils.ets","new_string":{"$blob":"sha256:4ef6df3dfee455597636588c83a7c839ca4e643466914c873ecbfe59c9c2e4f6","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":125,"compression":"none"},"old_string":{"$blob":"sha256:8fffa833ec64760bfb03f821a9ac32c3db1b9b179c27e625dbec0fdce3357618","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":79,"compression":"none"}},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"relativePath":"entry/src/main/ets/common/utils/play/FMUtils.ets","absolutePath":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec34/entry/src/main/ets/common/utils/play/FMUtils.ets","resolution":"absolute","content":{"$blob":"sha256:50466123209bd5eb69d28f040b86301da9b9ac0a69e7b5c9c28ccc9b6566ec3c","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":14894,"compression":"none"},"originalContent":{"$blob":"sha256:75822fec65379cddcda0a4ac7a436a2a9e4a5aca9870b31233c64e882167675c","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":14848,"compression