cond legitimate E1. This seems plausible since the unauthenticated server returns from a small song pool, and across many dislike tests the blacklist and persisted queue history have grown large, making duplicates more likely to surface in later tests.\n\nSo the \"≤1 logical request\" assertion feels too strict given this dedup/retry behavior. One fix is to count operations rather than raw requests — prefetch op plus a fallback on-demand op only when prefetch yields nothing. I'm also wondering whether unbounded history-based exclusion is really correct long-term, but it matches spec. To make the test more robust, I could add an explicit log line when prefetch completes with no usable song, so the test can distinguish a legitimate fallback fetch from an actual duplicate bug.\n\nI think I'll verify this by running test_04 and immediately pulling the hilog output right after to check if the pattern actually matches my hypothesis.\n\n","startTime":1792313658687,"lastModifiedTime":1792313670730},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01WyA7VE2uXdnFa1RwsfKB3N","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"cd /Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec34/logs && COMMON=\"$(cd ../../common && pwd)\" && PROJ=\"$(cd .. && pwd)\" && export PATH=/Applications/DevEco-Studio.app/Contents/sdk/default/openharmony/toolchains:$PATH && PYTHONPATH=\"$COMMON/test-harness:$PROJ\" \"$COMMON/.venv/bin/python\" -m unittest hypium_tests.test_04_persist.TestFMPersist.test_04_auto_next_after_complete 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(OK|FAILED|AssertionError)\"; hdc -t 127.0.0.1:5555 shell \"hilog -x -D 0x1010\" | grep -aE \"Request|Retry|FMUtils|AVPlayerUtils\" | cut -c7-200 | tail -12","description":"Rerun auto-next test and capture request log immediately","justification":"是否允许重跑自动续播用例并读取 hilog？","prefix_rule":"[\"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/common/.venv/bin/python\"]","sandbox_permissions":"require_escalated"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nEx