'm adding a dedupe guard in FMUtils so a completion event for the same song only triggers once, tracking the started song's ID and ignoring repeat completions for it.\n\nBut this exposes an edge case: if a user re-selects the same song after it finishes, its new completion would be wrongly ignored since the ID matches the stale completedSongId. The fix is to reset completedSongId whenever a new playback starts (even for the same song), so the sequence works correctly as songs transition. There's still a timing risk if the duplicate 'completed' event for song A arrives after the next song B has already started, which could wrongly suppress B's own completion — though the logs suggest the duplicate fires too quickly (0.17s) for that to happen before B's URL is even fetched.\n\nI'll limit this dedupe fix to FM mode only, leaving normal playback completion logic untouched, and wire it into the FM branch via FMUtils.onCompleted().\n\n","startTime":1792314352293,"lastModifiedTime":1792314363965},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01MabAascPryfyYfGkFZACi4","type":"TOOL","toolName":"edit_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec34/entry/src/main/ets/common/utils/play/FMUtils.ets","new_string":{"$blob":"sha256:d9a082ece01cd098a4d5f7f478d1580ee4075596cfba9d340ce15ac8631fbbbe","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":559,"compression":"none"},"old_string":{"$blob":"sha256:4ef6df3dfee455597636588c83a7c839ca4e643466914c873ecbfe59c9c2e4f6","version":1,"encoding":"utf8","byteLength":125,"compression":"none"}},"toolState":"cancelled","result":{"output":"Tool execution aborted","metadata":{"relativePath":"entry/src/main/ets/common/utils/play/FMUtils.ets","absolutePath":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec34/entry/src/main/ets/common/utils/play/FMUtils.ets","resolution":"absolute","success":false}},"accepted":true,"isRebuilt":false},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_019KYTM3Ydp1ChH8yiosEi8M","type":"TOOL","toolName":"edit_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/